``` SR-04 | Long-Running Searches Right Now, and Which to Kill
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: The cluster is slow at this moment; list every search currently
    running, how long it has been running, who owns it, and what it is
    scanning, so the right sid can be cancelled.
    Run on: SH-local. This shows only jobs dispatched from the search head you
    are logged into.
    Query: Main query
```
| rest splunk_server=local /services/search/jobs count=0
| search dispatchState=RUNNING OR dispatchState=FINALIZING
| eval run_min=round(runDuration / 60, 1),
       disk_mb=round(diskUsage / 1024 / 1024, 1),
       app='eai:acl.app',
       spl=substr(title, 1, 120)
| table sid author app label isSavedSearch run_min scanCount eventCount
        disk_mb earliestTime latestTime spl
| sort - run_min
